 she's  acting more like she runs a place  putting Blanc on edge Blanc tries to  stop the ritual but fails when Marcos  attacks her nearly decapitating her with  telepathic magic spraying blood  everywhere  with Blanc sidelined it seems like  marcos's Resurrection is imminent but it  turns out that the ceremony isn't for  her rebirth at all instead the ritual is  a combination of a power play from an  even stronger witch that's been brewing  in the background the whole film tearing  her flesh open Susie reveals herself to  be none other than the revived mother  superiorum the Millennia old entity who  was a founding member of The Witches  occult order Susie or now suspirioreum  begins to unleash bloody hella Marcos  and their allies in the coven who dare  to seize power in her place she doesn't  do it alone instead she summons a living  embodiment of death itself the stroll  around the room making your enemies  heads explode it's pretty trippy after  Marcos and her followers are dispatched  the rest of the movie is essentially  Susie's Victory lap she spares the lives  of the dancers as well as the witches  who weren't loyal to Mother Marcus and  also allows Patricia Sarah and Olga to  finally die their ruined bodies  collapsing to the ground at an act of  motherly Mercy it's a completely  different take on the original Suspiria  story and if the movie's cryptic  post-credits scene is to be believed the  story might just be getting started the  original Suspiria directed by Dario  Argento had two sequels Inferno and the  mother of Tears each focusing on a  different one of the powerful witches  known as the three mothers is it  possible that the Remake director Luca  guardanino is explicitly teasing sequels  in the vein of argento's follow-ups  while nothing's been announced yet it is  possible but don't worry too much about  decoding that cryptic last shot  according to screenwriter David kaganich  the brief scene of Susie standing in the  cold making vague gestures wasn't even  scripted most likely the scene is just  open to interpretation and meant to send  the viewers out of the theater thinking  talking and weighing the ending's  implications with a heavy sigh
 

